    description: "HPE Networking Instant On 1960 | JL805A#ABA The Instant On 1960 JL805A#ABA is a high-performance 24-port 10G smart managed switch designed to meet the growing connectivity demands of medium to large-sized businesses. With Power over Ethernet (PoE++) capabilities, this switch delivers both power and data over a single Ethernet cable, simplifying the deployment of access points, IP cameras, VoIP phones, and other network devices. The robust hardware and software capabilities ensure reliable, high-speed connectivity, making it ideal for supporting bandwidth-intensive applications such as video streaming and cloud services. The switch features comprehensive VLAN support for seamless network segmentation, optimizing traffic management and enhancing security. With Quality of Service (QoS), network administrators can prioritize critical traffic, ensuring smooth performance for latency-sensitive applications like voice and video conferencing. In addition, the Instant On 1960 JL805A#ABA incorporates advanced security features such as 802.1X authentication, Access Control Lists (ACLs), and strong encryption protocols to protect the network from unauthorized access and potential security threats. Offering cloud-based management, the Instant On 1960 JL805A#ABA allows for easy, remote configuration and monitoring, giving administrators full control over network settings and performance from any location. Its stacking capability supports network expansion as your business grows, providing scalability without compromising performance. Whether you are upgrading an existing network or creating a new infrastructure, this switch delivers the performance, security, and flexibility that modern businesses require for seamless operations. Smart Switch 1960 and Access Point The Instant On 1960 JL805A#ABA Smart Managed Switch integrates seamlessly with access points to provide a robust and efficient network infrastructure. Here’s how it works with access points: High-Speed Connectivity The 24 10G Ethernet ports on the JL805A#ABA deliver ultra-fast, reliable connections to access points, ensuring that they provide high-performance wireless coverage across the entire network. This is essential for businesses requiring strong, uninterrupted Wi-Fi performance. Power over Ethernet (PoE++) With PoE++ support, the switch can power access points and other network devices like IP cameras and VoIP phones through a single Ethernet cable. This makes installation easier by eliminating the need for separate power supplies and allowing for flexible placement of access points for optimal coverage. VLAN Segmentation The switch supports VLANs, allowing administrators to create separate virtual networks for different traffic types. Access points can be assigned to dedicated VLANs, improving security and performance by isolating guest and business traffic, ensuring network efficiency and data protection. Quality of Service (QoS) QoS features prioritize traffic from access points, ensuring that bandwidth-heavy applications such as video streaming or VoIP calls receive sufficient resources. This minimizes network delays and ensures smooth operation, even in high-demand environments. Cloud-Based Management The cloud management platform provides administrators with the ability to monitor and configure both the switch and connected access points remotely. This allows for easy troubleshooting, updates, and adjustments to network settings from anywhere. Enhanced Security Advanced security features such as 802.1X authentication and Access Control Lists (ACLs) help control which devices can connect to the network through access points, preventing unauthorized access and securing wireless communications. Scalability With stacking capability, the switch can support additional switches and access points, allowing the network to scale as the business grows. This ensures that network expansion can be handled efficiently without sacrificing performance. By offering PoE++, high-speed connectivity, VLAN support, and cloud-based management, the Instant On 1960 JL805A#ABA ensures access points deliver top-notch wireless coverage, security, and performance across the business network.",
