    description: "HPE Networking Instant On 1960 | JL807A#ABAThe Instant On 1960 JL807A#ABA is a top-tier 48-port 10G smart managed switch designed to deliver exceptional speed and reliability for medium to large-sized business networks. Featuring Power over Ethernet (PoE++), this switch efficiently powers and connects network devices such as access points, IP cameras, and VoIP phones through a single Ethernet cable, simplifying installations and enhancing network flexibility.This switch offers robust VLAN support, allowing for advanced network segmentation to optimize traffic flow and enhance security. With Quality of Service (QoS) capabilities, it prioritizes critical network traffic, ensuring that high-demand applications like video conferencing and VoIP operate smoothly without interruptions. Enhanced security features such as 802.1X authentication and Access Control Lists (ACLs) protect your network from unauthorized access and potential threats.The Instant On 1960 JL807A#ABA comes with cloud-based management, enabling remote configuration and monitoring of the switch and connected devices, which simplifies network administration. Its stacking capability ensures that as your business grows, the network can scale efficiently to meet increasing demands without compromising performance. Whether upgrading your existing infrastructure or setting up a new network, this switch offers the performance, security, and flexibility needed to support dynamic business environments. Smart Switch 1960 and Access Point The Instant On 1960 JL807A#ABA Smart Managed Switch effectively integrates with access points to provide robust and efficient network connectivity. Here’s how it works with access points:High-Speed ConnectivityThe 48 10G Ethernet ports on the JL807A#ABA offer high-speed connections to access points, ensuring fast and reliable wireless coverage throughout your business environment. This supports demanding applications and large numbers of wireless clients.Power over Ethernet (PoE++)The switch provides PoE++, allowing it to deliver both power and data to access points through a single Ethernet cable. This eliminates the need for separate power supplies and allows for flexible placement of access points to maximize wireless coverage and performance.VLAN SupportWith VLAN capabilities, the JL807A#ABA allows you to segment your network into separate virtual networks. Access points can be assigned to different VLANs to isolate and manage traffic effectively, enhancing both security and network performance by segregating guest and internal business traffic.Quality of Service (QoS)The switch’s QoS features ensure that traffic from access points is prioritized based on application requirements. This is crucial for maintaining high performance for latency-sensitive applications like video calls and online gaming, even in high-traffic environments.Cloud-Based ManagementCloud-based management enables remote monitoring and configuration of the switch and connected access points from anywhere. This simplifies network administration, allowing for quick adjustments and troubleshooting without needing physical access to the equipment.Enhanced SecurityThe switch includes advanced security features such as 802.1X authentication and Access Control Lists (ACLs). These features help secure the network by controlling access and preventing unauthorized connections through access points.ScalabilityThe stacking capability of the JL807A#ABA supports network expansion. As your network grows and more access points are added, the switch can accommodate increased traffic and ensure consistent performance.By providing PoE++, high-speed connectivity, VLAN support, QoS, and cloud-based management, the Instant On 1960 JL807A#ABA ensures that access points deliver efficient, secure, and high-performance wireless connectivity across your business network.",
