    name: "HPE Networking Instant On 1930 24-Port Gb Ethernet 24xGE, 4X 1G, 10G SFP+, L2+ Smart Switch US Cord | JL682A#ABA",
    description: "HPE Networking Instant On 1930 | JL682A#ABAThe Instant On 1930 JL682A#ABA is a powerful 24-port Gigabit Ethernet smart managed switch designed to deliver reliable, high-speed connectivity for small and medium-sized businesses. With features like Power over Ethernet (PoE), this switch simplifies network setups by providing both data and power to devices such as access points and IP cameras through a single cable. The switch’s intuitive web-based interface makes it easy to configure and manage, even for users without extensive networking expertise.This switch supports VLAN capabilities, allowing network administrators to segment traffic for improved security and efficiency. With 802.1X authentication, Access Control Lists (ACLs), and advanced Quality of Service (QoS) features, the Instant On 1930 ensures secure and prioritized data flow, reducing network congestion and protecting against unauthorized access. Its advanced security protocols are essential for safeguarding sensitive business information and maintaining a safe network environment.Designed to grow with your business, the Instant On 1930 JL682A#ABA supports stacking, enabling seamless scalability as your networking needs expand. Its high-performance design ensures the switch can handle increasing traffic demands while maintaining stable and fast connectivity. Whether you're looking to enhance your current infrastructure or prepare for future network growth, this switch offers the flexibility and reliability needed to keep your business connected. Smart Switch 1930 and Access Point The Instant On 1930 JL682A#ABA Smart Managed Switch works seamlessly with access points to enhance network performance, security, and management. Here’s how it integrates with access points:Gigabit ConnectivityThe switch provides Gigabit Ethernet ports that ensure high-speed connections to access points, supporting fast and reliable data transfer. This allows access points to offer seamless wireless performance to connected devices, reducing latency and improving overall network efficiency.Power over Ethernet (PoE)With PoE support, the Instant On 1930 can supply both power and data to access points through a single Ethernet cable. This simplifies the installation process by eliminating the need for separate power sources, making it easier to deploy access points in locations where power outlets are limited.VLAN SupportThe switch’s VLAN capabilities allow you to segment traffic by assigning different VLANs to access points. For example, you can create separate VLANs for guest Wi-Fi, employee devices, and IoT equipment. This improves security and optimizes network performance by keeping traffic isolated and efficiently managed.Quality of Service (QoS)The Instant On 1930 offers QoS features that prioritize critical network traffic. This ensures that high-priority tasks such as video streaming, voice calls, or business-critical applications receive the necessary bandwidth, even when multiple access points are in use.Advanced SecuritySecurity features like 802.1X authentication and Access Control Lists (ACLs) work with access points to protect against unauthorized access. These security measures ensure that only authorized users and devices can connect to the network through the access points, safeguarding sensitive data.Centralized ManagementThrough its cloud-based management platform, the switch allows network administrators to manage connected access points remotely. You can configure, monitor, and troubleshoot both the switch and the access points from a single dashboard, providing centralized control and simplifying network maintenance.Scalability and FlexibilityThe Instant On 1930 supports stacking, allowing it to easily integrate additional switches and access points as your network grows. This makes it an ideal solution for businesses looking to scale their wireless network without complicated setups.The Instant On 1930 JL682A#ABA Smart Switch enhances access point functionality by providing high-speed connectivity, PoE support, network segmentation, security, traffic prioritization, and centralized management, ensuring efficient and scalable wireless networking for businesses.",
