    name: "HPE Networking Instant On AP22 802.11ax 2x2 Wi-Fi 6 Wireless Access Point | US Model | Power Source Included | R6M49A",
    description: "HPE Networking Instant On AP22 | R6M49AThe Instant On AP22 is a cutting-edge wireless access point designed to deliver exceptional performance and coverage for small to medium-sized businesses and high-demand home environments. Featuring advanced dual-band 802.11ax (Wi-Fi 6) technology, the AP22 provides blazing-fast speeds of up to 2.4 Gbps, ensuring smooth and reliable connectivity for all your devices, whether you're streaming, gaming, or working remotely.With its sleek and compact design, the AP22 integrates seamlessly into any environment, offering versatile mounting options to fit your space. The access point supports Power over Ethernet (PoE), simplifying installation by allowing both power and data to be delivered through a single Ethernet cable. Advanced security features, including WPA3 encryption, help protect your network from unauthorized access, while guest network capabilities ensure a secure and isolated connection for visitors.Management is straightforward with the Instant On mobile app or web portal, allowing you to easily configure, monitor, and optimize your network from anywhere. The AP22 is built to handle high-density environments, providing reliable coverage even in areas with numerous connected devices. Ideal for enhancing network performance in offices, retail spaces, and other business settings, the Instant On AP22 combines cutting-edge technology with ease of use to deliver an outstanding networking experience. Access Point AP22 and Smart Switch The Instant On AP22 works effectively with smart switches to enhance network performance and management. Here’s how it integrates with smart switches:Network IntegrationThe Instant On AP22 connects to a smart switch to extend both wired and wireless network capabilities. This integration allows the AP22 to distribute internet connectivity efficiently throughout a space, leveraging the switch to manage traffic and optimize performance.Power over Ethernet (PoE)The AP22 supports Power over Ethernet (PoE), which means it can receive both power and data through a single Ethernet cable connected to a PoE-enabled smart switch. This simplifies installation by reducing the need for additional power sources and cables.VLAN SupportSmart switches often support Virtual LANs (VLANs), which can segregate network traffic for improved performance and security. The AP22 can be configured to work with these VLANs, allowing you to create separate networks for different types of traffic, such as separating guest Wi-Fi from business-critical applications.Traffic ManagementSmart switches often have Quality of Service (QoS) features to prioritize network traffic. When used with the AP22, the smart switch can manage and prioritize different types of traffic, ensuring that high-bandwidth activities like video streaming or VoIP calls receive the necessary bandwidth and low latency.Centralized ManagementBoth the AP22 and the smart switch can be managed through centralized network management tools, such as the Instant On mobile app or web portal. This allows for easy configuration, monitoring, and troubleshooting of the entire network, providing a streamlined approach to network management.Enhanced SecurityIntegrating the AP22 with a smart switch enhances network security. For example, you can use the smart switch to set up VLANs that isolate guest network traffic from sensitive business data, and the AP22 will adhere to these security protocols to protect network integrity.ScalabilityAs your network grows, the AP22 and smart switch combination allows for easy scalability. You can add more AP22 units or other network devices without significant reconfiguration, as the smart switch can handle additional traffic and manage multiple access points efficiently.The Instant On AP22 works with smart switches to provide a comprehensive and scalable network solution. By leveraging PoE, VLAN support, traffic management, and centralized management, this setup ensures robust performance, efficient traffic handling, and enhanced security for various network environments.",
